        "32": "Page 32 | Greenwood College School Annual Report 2025\u20132026\nGreenwood Circle\nThe Greenwood Circle is our annual donor recognition society, acknowledging the \nphilanthropy of current and past parents and guardians, alumni, staff and friends \nwho generously support the school each year. Individuals qualified for the 2025-2026 \nGreenwood Circle by donating $2,000 or more between July 1, 2025 and June 30, \n2026. The Circle\u2019s giving societies are named for Canada\u2019s great parks, in recognition \nof Greenwood\u2019s commitment to the outdoors and the environment.\nThe Banff Society ($25K+)\nSandra and Graeme Hepworth\nThe Hazelton Lane Family\nThe Martin Family\nHeather and John McCallum\nThe Nahanni Society ($10K+)\nThe Botha Family\nThe Chapnik Family \nThe Hawkey Family \nThe Huang Family\nThe Janson Family\nJennifer and Jason Peel\nThe Langar Foundation\nThe Malhotra Family\nThe McLachlan Family\nThe Family of Noah Venn-Mitchell \u201816\nArianne Purves Mitchell and Scott Mitchell\nJulia West and Richard Wernham\nSarah Farrugia and Christopher Parisien\nThe Pepper Family\nThe Etches / Raheel Family\nThe Waghmare Family \nThe Sadeh and Ward Family\nJulie Coleman and Mark Wayne\nKellie Smith and Glenn Zujew\n\u2026 and one anonymous donor\nThe Algonquin Society ($5K+)\nElizabeth Koester and Stephen Bowman\nThe Dravers Family \nLisa and Brian Dymond\nThe Gidney Family\nThe Fleming Family \nThe Gosevitz-Foulds Family\nTiffany Tan and Matthew Kohler \nNoreen Halpern and Kevin Murphy\nAudrey and Jason Kim\nDavid Rogan\nLindsay Rogan and John Scott\nRebecca and Jeffrey Tannenbaum \nThe Veneziano Family\nThe Terra Nova Society ($3.5K+)\nThe Botting Family\nThe Majeed / Bryant Family\nThe Goldmans\nSarah Mitchell and Keith Liu\nCindy Patrino and Fred Nastos \nMarcia McLean and Sumit Oberai\n",
